WEBVTT

00:00:06.892 --> 00:00:08.265
<v><b>Ned:</b></v> Hi, I’m Ned.

00:00:08.452 --> 00:00:10.564
Welcome to Portchester Castle.

00:00:18.455 --> 00:00:22.490
Portchester Castle is over one thousand seven hundred years old.

00:00:22.797 --> 00:00:26.400
It’s near Portsmouth, a city on the south coast of England.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:32.887
The castle is part of English Heritage.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:40.611
English Heritage is a charity, which manages over four hundred old buildings and monuments in England.

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:46.546
With so many old buildings, there are also lots of reports of ghosts.

00:00:46.852 --> 00:00:52.697
And ghosts are sometimes a problem for staff members and visitors at English Heritage.

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:59.192
In fact, some staff members decided to leave their jobs because of the ghosts.

00:01:01.156 --> 00:01:08.120
I’ve come here to Portchester to find out more about reports of not one, but four ghosts!

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:13.097
And many of the ghosts come from different times in Portchester’s long history.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.639
Portchester Castle dates back to Roman Britain;

00:01:24.287 --> 00:01:28.170
the Romans built the original castle here in the year two hundred and ninety.

00:01:30.157 --> 00:01:33.747
The first ghost report also comes from Roman times.

00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:39.955
Visitors report that they see the ghost of a Roman soldier guarding the walls,

00:01:40.436 --> 00:01:43.401
but they say they don’t feel frightened.

00:01:47.662 --> 00:01:52.912
In the Middle Ages, Portchester became a favorite castle for the kings and queens of England.

00:01:54.485 --> 00:01:57.653
During this time, a small monastery was built.

00:02:02.938 --> 00:02:06.024
There’s a church here now in place of the monastery.

00:02:06.343 --> 00:02:10.387
People say that they see a man dressed in black here and

00:02:10.388 --> 00:02:13.818
they think he is the ghost of a monk from the monastery.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.559
Surprisingly, people don’t feel frightened when they see him.

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:21.387
They say that he disappears when they look at him.

00:02:24.623 --> 00:02:27.275
Our first two ghosts are not frightening,

00:02:27.422 --> 00:02:31.663
but the next ghost really frightens people – the White Lady.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.230
Some people believe that this is the ghost of Charlotte White.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:51.990
She was a woman who visited the castle in the nineteenth century.

00:02:52.736 --> 00:03:00.480
Charlotte’s baby fell into the water and poor Charlotte also died when she tried to save her child.

00:03:02.876 --> 00:03:07.042
The most frightening ghost of all is a man on a black horse.

00:03:07.895 --> 00:03:11.905
Both castle visitors and staff members say that they see him.

00:03:12.356 --> 00:03:14.700
One of the staff who saw the ghost said,

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:22.354
“It got bigger and bigger. It started to come towards me and I screamed and ran away.”

00:03:24.005 --> 00:03:27.051
People also say they hear the sound of horses;

00:03:27.218 --> 00:03:31.954
one visitor even heard the sound of horses on a video he filmed.

00:03:33.314 --> 00:03:36.613
One of the strange things about the man on the horse is that

00:03:36.614 --> 00:03:42.214
we don’t know who he is or which part of Portchester’s long history he is from.

00:03:48.457 --> 00:03:52.476
I was sure I didn’t believe in ghosts before I came here,

00:03:52.477 --> 00:03:57.184
but, after a day at Portchester, I’m not so sure.